      "kind": "claim",
      "title": "Even a split quotient need not admit a natural selection-preserving section transfer",
      "body": "A section transfer is natural under source automorphisms over H only if its section is fixed by Aut_H(G). Such an invariant section need not exist even when group-homomorphic sections exist; therefore abstract splitting does not canonically supply the transfer.",
      "entity_id": "claim:60f6e26ad2eba35bcb9a"
    },
    {
      "op": "entity.declare",
      "local_ref": "test",
      "kind": "test",
      "title": "C2×C2->C2 no-natural-section hostile control",
      "body": "There are exactly two identity-preserving group-homomorphic sections. The base-preserving shear (a,b)->(a,a+b) swaps them, so the automorphism-natural section count is zero. All assertions pass.",
      "entity_id": "test:25c031a9f3b1ba1c795b"
